{
  "case_id": "2006-06-969",
  "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Election Commission",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In McConnell against FEC this Court upheld Title II's restrictions on electioneering communications by unions and corporations against facial attack. In doing so, this Court reviewed a voluminous record and concluded that the vast majority of the ads that had been run in previous cycles and came within the statutory definition could constitutionally be regulated by Congress. Accordingly, this Court rejected the overbreadth challenge and upheld the statute on it face."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, did that statement refer only to issue ads, or did it refer to all ads?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court. I'd like to -- I'd like to address three points that came up at the earlier part of the argument. First of all, I'd like to, I think just with respect correct a premise of one of Justice Scalia's questions. Then I would like to address the two questions that I think I heard the Chief Justice ask, which is how do we know that the this is an atypical ad, and what would the standard -- what standard would a court apply in adjudicating as-applied challenges? And then finally, assuming there's time permitting I'd like to address the question of why we shouldn't revisit McConnell which I think was posed both by the Chief Justice and by Justice Scalia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That vast majority thing, is that a -- was that the holding of the case? I mean"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "ACLU",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to give you the ACLU as an example because many -- their brief is quite powerful. They and the other amici who provide a growing table of amicus briefs every time this issue comes up, have never, ever, brought their own as-applied challenge"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But doesn't any communication depend upon the understanding of the listener? Can we even sensibly talk about what a statement means or an advertisement means without understanding the context in terms of the listener's understanding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: When they put these exhibits, were those exhibits complete with context?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why should those things be ignored?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You think they're dumb?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bopp",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's absolutely no evidence that anyone in Wisconsin knew his position on the filibuster."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's pretty easy to tell whether you're giving money to the money to the candidate or not, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you trying to convince us the purpose of these ads was to convince Senator Feingold to change his position on filibusters?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bopp",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was indeed. It was to lobby him about the upcoming vote."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that called democracy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you agree that the Constitution permits Congress to pass a statute that prohibits your using electioneering ads that use magic words?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You think that is protected?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Does that go to their meaning or to the intent of -- is that what governs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: No. Our position is slightly different than intervenors on that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: It could be as long as 200 days; isn't that correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How long will the blackout period be during the upcoming year for the presidential candidates?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bopp",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOPP: Well, I think that in various places it will be 30 days before the primary and then obviously 60 days before the general."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9040d0be526636a88f942bc2c251521e712b0375b96ecea746006858e44841db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9040d0be5266-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: No, they don't, Justice Scalia, and one of the arguments that's made to try to suggest that there should be a reconsideration of McConnell is, as-applied checks don't work."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-969",
      "confidence": 0.0,
